--- Functions put in a list one at a time (`fs = push[fs, sq]`) are typed
--- by the calls made through the list's items — an item read into a local
--- and called, one called where it is read (`fs[0][5]`), or a loop's
--- variable called — as functions in a list written down are: refused as
--- functions nothing calls, they had run only where the program also
--- called them directly (Rosetta Code, Closures/Value capture).
fn sq[i]
    return i * i

fn cube[i]
    return i * i * i

fs = push[[], sq]
fs = push[fs, cube]
g = fs[1]
log[g[4]]
for f in fs
    log[f[3]]
log[fs[0][5]]
